            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for one's own (by birth), then the Mandarin for personally (doing it oneself)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: zhìxiàng",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhìxiàng — \"ambition in life; the goal one sets oneself\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "wǒ zuì dà de zhìxiàng shì dāng yīshēng — My greatest ambition is to be a doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhìxiàng is built from zhì 'a longing' and xiàng 'to face', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsyiH and xjangH (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'what the mind longs for' and the second 'to face'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying how it was."
